==Classical Nahuatl==
{{was fwotd|2015|February|23|lang=nci}}
[[Image:Calli.jpg|thumb|right|The [[glyph]] for the day sign ''calli'' “house”, from the [[w:Codex Magliabechiano|Codex Magliabechiano]].]]

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|nci|azc-nah-pro}}, from {{inh|nci|azc-pro|*kaliR}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{IPA|[ˈka.lːi]|lang=nci}}

====Noun====
{{nci-noun|i}}

# an enclosed [[habitation]]al space, a [[house]] or [[room]]
#* '''1555''', [[w:Alonso de Molina|Alonso de Molina]], ''[[w:Aquí comiença un vocabulario en la lengua castellana y mexicana|Aqui comienca vn vocabulario en la lengua castellana y mexicana]]'', f. 45v.
#*: Caſa. &nbsp;&nbsp;'''calli'''.techan.
#*:: A house. '''calli'''. techan.
#* '''1571''', ''Idem'', ''[[w:Vocabulario en lengua castellana y mexicana y mexicana y castellana|Vocabulario en lengua castellana y mexicana y mexicana y castellana]]'', f. 25r. col. 2.
#*: Caſa. '''calli'''. techan.
#*:: A house. '''calli'''. techan.
#* ''Idem'', f. 11v. col. 1.
#*: '''Calli'''. caſa, o tenazuelas de palo o de caña para / comer mayz toſtado enel reſcoldo.
#*:: '''Calli'''. a house, or small wooden or cane tongs used to eat maize that has toasted on embers.
# the third [[day sign]] of the [[Aztec]] {{m|nci|tōnalpōhualli}}, represented conceptually by a stylized one-room house
#* '''16C''', ''[[w:Codex Magliabechiano|Codex Magliabechiano]]'', f. 11v.
#*: chico açe '''cale''' / q̃ quiere dezir / seis casas.
#*:: chico açe '''cale'''. <small>[sic]</small> which means “six houses”.

